    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1055">

                <pb facs="0974" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/711</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McAdoo</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department</hi>, <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-27">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">October 27, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For your consideration in connection with
                    this Department’s letter of the 26th instant, relative to the Japanese
                    battleship <hi rendition="#italic">Hizen</hi>, I have the honor to communicate
                    further cablegrams from the collector of customs at Honolulu, as follows:</p>
                <p>Honolulu, October 26, 1914, 5:45 p.m. Captain Brown of the revenue cutter <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thetis</hi> reports that steam launches from the
                    Japanese battleship <hi rendition="#italic">Hizen</hi> were again in neutral
                    waters last night without lights.</p>
                <p>Honolulu, October 26, 1914, 12:45 p.m. Captain <hi rendition="#italic">Hisen</hi>
                    desires to send sealed communications to the Japanese consul and receive sealed
                    replies. Await instructions.</p>
                <p>By direction of the Secretary,</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">B. R. Newton</hi>, <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Secretary</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
